{
  "about": "Search parity fixture (#112). Every frontend builds an index of `files` under a fresh root, scans `apps` under the same root, treats the root as the home folder, and checks each query's publication. `rows` is the expected head of the list, in order; `absent` titles must not appear; `counts` are the chip counts; the web row is always last.",
